{"type":"message","id":"5c9b61b8","parentId":"6836f98c","timestamp":"2026-10-05T17:24:39.981Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_nVsyKSZoxn5C4B4NH7XXPQSq|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac3dd57c08887d094836489a5f445ca","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"pr\": 212,\n  \"head\": \"0680df1ee45cd4797f574bc99489d2dc1d1532ca\",\n  \"threads\": 31,\n  \"primary\": 8,\n  \"files\": 75,\n  \"checks\": [\n    [\n      \"GitGuardian Security Checks\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"SonarCloud Code Analysis\",\n      \"failure\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Graphite / AI Reviews\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"CodeQL\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"McpFn release gate\",\n      \"skipped\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"McpFn Node 18 CommonJS\",\n      \"skipped\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"McpFn Node 20 compatibility\",\n      \"skipped\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Python (billfn, billfn/python)\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Python (datafn, datafn/python)\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Python (apifn, apifn/python)\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Python (filefn, filefn/python)\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Python (plugfn, plugfn/python)\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Python (superfunctions-fastapi, packages/python-fastapi)\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Python (superfunctions-sqlalchemy, packages/python-sqlalchemy)\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Python (authfn, authfn/python)\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Python (superfunctions-flask, packages/python-flask)\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Python (sendfn, sendfn/python)\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Python (searchfn, searchfn/python)\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"JavaScript\",\n      \"failure\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Python (superfunctions, packages/python-core)\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Socket Security: Pull Request Alerts\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"cubic \\u00b7 AI code reviewer\",\n      \"neutral\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Socket Security: Project Report\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Kody Code Review\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"pullfrog\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Analyze (javascript-typescript)\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Sourcery review\",\n      \"skipped\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"release-gate\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"test-node-18\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Plan\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"mailfn-release\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Analyze (swift)\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Analyze (python)\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Analyze (javascript-typescript)\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Analyze (rust)\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Analyze (actions)\",\n      \"success\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Analyze (python)\",\n      \"success\"\n    ]\n  ]\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791221079981}}
{"type":"message","id":"a0efede2","parentId":"5c9b61b8","timestamp":"2026-10-05T17:24:39.982Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_aOLBLfJ2yQiX4180OItwDj7Y|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac3dd57c0a087d09ca3e4da2d23c355","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNznn scripts/docs-site/Search.svelte\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Keep the search request under the deployed route**\n\nWhen this site is deployed through the repository's Cloudflare docs mechanism, `scripts/cloudflare-docs/config.mjs` attaches each docs worker only to `${host}/docs*`, so this root-level `/search.json` request bypasses the worker and search returns an error. Serve the endpoint below `/docs` (and fetch that URL), or explicitly include `/search.json` in the worker routes.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNzno devfn/docs/content/docs/lifecycle.md\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Document the machine state directory separately**\n\nThis says state is kept under the configured project runtime directory, but `defaultStateDir()` stores trust records, the port registry, lifecycle locks, and proxy state under `$XDG_STATE_HOME/devfn` (or `~/.local/state/devfn`); only receipts, logs, and generated runtime outputs default to `.devfn/`. Users following this lifecycle or cleanup guidance could therefore overlook the actual machine-level state.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mPowm scripts/docs-site/layout.ts\n## Superfluous trailing arguments\n\n<p>Superfluous argument passed to <a class=\"Link\" href=\"/21nCo/super-functions/blob/13f561830279b4c40c8d095f2fdd38ff4c719bfa/scripts/verify-uifn-react-18-runtime.mjs#L49-L49\">default constructor of anonymous class</a>.</p>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mPqSc devfn/docs/package.json\n**Security issue**  \n🛑 Blocker — must fix before merge\n\n**Known vulnerabilities in vite@5.4.0**\n\nOSV.dev reports 15 known vulnerabilities affecting `vite@5.4.0`, introduced by this PR:\n\n- [GHSA-356w-63v5-8wf4](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-32395) **moderate**: Vite has an `server.fs.deny` bypass with an invalid `request-target` — fixed in 6.2.6, 6.1.5, 6.0.15, 5.4.18, 4.5.13\n- [GHSA-4r4m-qw57-chr8](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-31125) **moderate**: Vite has a `server.fs.deny` bypassed for `inline` and `raw` with `?import` query — fixed in 6.2.4, 6.1.3, 6.0.13, 5.4.16, 4.5.11\n- [GHSA-4w7w-66w2-5vf9](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-39365) **moderate**: Vite Vulnerable to Path Traversal in Optimized Deps `.map` Handling — fixed in 8.0.5, 7.3.2, 6.4.2\n\n…and 12 more — see the OSV links above.\n\nUpgrade to 6.2.6, 6.1.5, 6.0.15, 5.4.18, 4.5.13 or later.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn devfn/docs/package.json, upgrade the dependency vite from 5.4.0 to a non-vulnerable version (0.1.24, 2.14.1, 2.9.0, 3.2.11, 4.5.10, 4.5.11, 4.5.12, 4.5.13, 4.5.14, 4.5.4, 4.5.6, 5.2.14, 5.3.6, 5.4.12, 5.4.15, 5.4.16, 5.4.17, 5.4.18, 5.4.19, 5.4.20, 5.4.21, 5.4.6, 5.4.9, 6.0.12, 6.0.13, 6.0.14, 6.0.15, 6.0.9, 6.1.2, 6.1.3, 6.1.4, 6.1.5, 6.1.6, 6.2.3, 6.2.4, 6.2.5, 6.2.6, 6.2.7, 6.3.4, 6.3.6, 6.4.1, 6.4.2, 6.4.3, 7.0.7, 7.0.8, 7.1.11, 7.1.5, 7.3.2, 7.3.5, 8.0.16, 8.0.5). Update any associated lockfile entries.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n> Not useful? Reply `@mira-rhombus reject` to dismiss this suggestion.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mP2wk devfn/docs/package.json\n**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Register DevFn with the docs deployment pipeline**\n\nThe new `@devfn/docs` workspace cannot be deployed by the repository's Cloudflare docs tooling: `scripts/cloudflare-docs/config.mjs` has no `devfn` product, `select-products.mjs` never selects changes under `devfn/docs`, and the deploy workflow neither watches that directory nor offers DevFn as a product. Confirmed by running `node scripts/cloudflare-docs/deploy.mjs dev --products=devfn --dry-run --skip-build`, which exits with `Invalid docs product: devfn`; register the product and add the corresponding workflow paths/options so this site can reach its documented public URL.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mP28x devfn/docs/package.json\n**Security issue**  \n🛑 Blocker — must fix before merge\n\n**Known vulnerabilities in vite@5.4.0**\n\nOSV.dev reports 15 known vulnerabilities affecting `vite@5.4.0`, introduced by this PR:\n\n- [GHSA-356w-63v5-8wf4](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-32395) **moderate**: Vite has an `server.fs.deny` bypass with an invalid `request-target` — fixed in 6.2.6, 6.1.5, 6.0.15, 5.4.18, 4.5.13\n- [GHSA-4r4m-qw57-chr8](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-31125) **moderate**: Vite has a `server.fs.deny` bypassed for `inline` and `raw` with `?import` query — fixed in 6.2.4, 6.1.3, 6.0.13, 5.4.16, 4.5.11\n- [GHSA-4w7w-66w2-5vf9](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-39365) **moderate**: Vite Vulnerable to Path Traversal in Optimized Deps `.map` Handling — fixed in 8.0.5, 7.3.2, 6.4.2\n\n…and 12 more — see the OSV links above.\n\nUpgrade to 6.2.6, 6.1.5, 6.0.15, 5.4.18, 4.5.13 or later.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn devfn/docs/package.json, upgrade the dependency vite from 5.4.0 to a non-vulnerable version (0.1.24, 2.14.1, 2.9.0, 3.2.11, 4.5.10, 4.5.11, 4.5.12, 4.5.13, 4.5.14, 4.5.4, 4.5.6, 5.2.14, 5.3.6, 5.4.12, 5.4.15, 5.4.16, 5.4.17, 5.4.18, 5.4.19, 5.4.20, 5.4.21, 5.4.6, 5.4.9, 6.0.12, 6.0.13, 6.0.14, 6.0.15, 6.0.9, 6.1.2, 6.1.3, 6.1.4, 6.1.5, 6.1.6, 6.2.3, 6.2.4, 6.2.5, 6.2.6, 6.2.7, 6.3.4, 6.3.6, 6.4.1, 6.4.2, 6.4.3, 7.0.7, 7.0.8, 7.1.11, 7.1.5, 7.3.2, 7.3.5, 8.0.16, 8.0.5). Update any associated lockfile entries.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n> Not useful? Reply `@mira-rhombus reject` to dismiss this suggestion.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6nFoqb .github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-deploy.yml\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Add DevFn to the route-sync workflow**\n\nSelecting this new DevFn deployment option only uploads the Worker; `deploy.mjs` does not attach the `devfn.com/docs*` route. Fresh evidence from the repo-wide workflow search is that `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-routes.yml` remains the route-provisioning mechanism, but its product choices and zone-ID environment variables omit DevFn, so operators cannot sync this product independently and the public route can remain unattached unless they resync every product via `all` or run the script manually.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6nkGqp scripts/docs-site/vitest.config.ts\n![kody code-review](https://img.shields.io/badge/kody-code--review-312B4B?labelColor=C9BBF2) ![Kody Rules](https://img.shields.io/badge/Kody_Rules-4527A0) ![medium](https://img.shields.io/badge/severity_level-medium-1A7BBE)\n\n\nImplicit `any` on `sitePackage`: the variable lacks a type annotation and inherits the `any` result of `JSON.parse`. Annotate it with an explicit shape (or cast through `unknown`) to satisfy the no-`any` type-safety rule and keep type checking strict.\n\nKody rule violation: [Disallow \\`any\\` type usage](https://app.kodus.io/settings/code-review/global/kody-rules/5ba5ce8d-2e90-425b-8ca3-6019f927f489?teamId=c7d4a17c-c2c8-426a-9c23-3048fd1d53b9)\n\n```typescript\nlet sitePackage: { name?: string; dependencies?: Record<string, string> };\n```\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Prompt for LLM</summary>\n\n```\n\nFile scripts/docs-site/vitest.config.ts:\n\nLine 9:\n\nImplicit `any` on `sitePackage`: the variable lacks a type annotation and inherits the `any` result of `JSON.parse`. Annotate it with an explicit shape (or cast through `unknown`) to satisfy the no-`any` type-safety rule and keep type checking strict.\n\nSuggested Code:\n\nlet sitePackage: { name?: string; dependencies?: Record<string, string> };\n\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n<sub>Talk to Kody by mentioning @kody</sub>\n\n\n<sub>Was this suggestion helpful? React with 👍 or 👎 to help Kody learn from this interaction.</sub>\n\n<!-- kody-codereview -->&#8203;\n&#8203;"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791221079982}}
{"type":"message","id":"f820e996","parentId":"a0efede2","timestamp":"2026-10-05T17:24:39.982Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_3VC9Tiqz1Qnpc7A9iTGPv13B|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac3dd57c0ac87d0a756277c55bd2ca8","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNncm resolved=True devfn/docs/content/docs/getting-started.md\n<!-- cubic:v=1575d896-a107-4270-ac1c-f686aabc2b64 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=ce14b52f-6485-5594-8298-c25e4d334624 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":10} -->\nP1: `init` only previews and does not write a manifest, so the following `doctor --trust` fails with `DEVFN_CONFIG_NOT_FOUND`. Add `init --yes` after reviewing the preview and before continuing.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At devfn/docs/content/docs/getting-started.md, line 11:\n\n<comment>`init` only previews and does not write a manifest, so the following `doctor --trust` fails with `DEVFN_CONFIG_NOT_FOUND`. Add `init --yes` after reviewing the preview and before continuing.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@\n+Install or invoke `@devfn/cli` from the repository you want to run. `init` previews detected configuration; review it before accepting generated files. The first load of any manifest needs `--trust`, even for JSON, because it can declare lifecycle commands. Trust is bound to the exact manifest digest, so an edit requires review and trust again.\n+\n+```sh\n+npx @devfn/cli init\n+npx @devfn/cli doctor --trust\n+npx @devfn/cli up --profile default\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\nnpx @devfn/cli init\nnpx @devfn/cli init --yes\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`aabb7d6`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/aabb7d6f0d3147d010d061f4a461ff1ba6d059a8)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNncp resolved=True devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/migration.md\n<!-- cubic:v=ad1673ee-4635-4324-9afd-65aded1f5e62 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=ce14b52f-6485-5594-8298-c25e4d334624 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP1: This does not ensure DevFn uses the existing database volume: its worktree-specific Compose project can select a different project-scoped volume, and `down` removes DevFn-created containers, losing data stored only in their writable layers. Tell adopters to verify the intended volume and back up container-only data before the first start.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/migration.md, line 15:\n\n<comment>This does not ensure DevFn uses the existing database volume: its worktree-specific Compose project can select a different project-scoped volume, and `down` removes DevFn-created containers, losing data stored only in their writable layers. Tell adopters to verify the intended volume and back up container-only data before the first start.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@\n+5. Before the first start, back up every pre-existing file targeted by `environmentOutputs[].path`; DevFn overwrites configured outputs and cannot restore prior contents.\n+6. Start with a minimal profile and compare it with the existing manual startup flow.\n+7. Add full, OAuth, test, or docs profiles incrementally. Public tunnels must remain explicit.\n+8. Verify `devfn down` preserves databases and volumes before adopting it as the daily command.\n+\n+Rollback by running `devfn down`, then inspect `runtimeDir` and every `environmentOutputs[].path` in the manifest before removing generated files. The default generated location is `.devfn/`, but custom paths may live elsewhere. Preserve any target that existed before DevFn adoption; cleanup does not know whether a configured output replaced user-owned content. Finally remove the DevFn manifest and continue using the preserved original scripts. Docker volumes and source configuration are not deleted.\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\n8. Before the first start, verify DevFn uses the intended database volume; its worktree-specific Compose project can select a new volume, and `devfn down` removes DevFn-created containers, losing data stored only in their writable layers.\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`13f5618`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/13f561830279b4c40c8d095f2fdd38ff4c719bfa)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNncs resolved=True devfn/docs/src/app.css\n<!-- cubic:v=69eacb6c-f9aa-496f-8acc-a72ba3f731b6 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=ce14b52f-6485-5594-8298-c25e4d334624 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP2: The sticky offset is disabled, so the docs sidebar and TOC can stick at the viewport top underneath the sticky TopBar. Enable the provided offset so both remain visible below it.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At devfn/docs/src/app.css, line 19:\n\n<comment>The sticky offset is disabled, so the docs sidebar and TOC can stick at the viewport top underneath the sticky TopBar. Enable the provided offset so both remain visible below it.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@\n+   * TopBar is outside DocsLayout but uses position:sticky in theme.css.\n+   * Set this to roughly the rendered top bar height so the docs sidebar/TOC stick below it.\n+   */\n+  /* --docsfn-sticky-top-offset: 2.7rem; */\n+\n+  /* Whole docs chrome (left sidebar + article + right TOC) max width; centers as a group */\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`13f5618`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/13f561830279b4c40c8d095f2fdd38ff4c719bfa)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNnct resolved=True devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/configuration.md\n<!-- cubic:v=0cbacab6-a009-4bc2-81fc-0c594b050ee8 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=ce14b52f-6485-5594-8298-c25e4d334624 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} -->\nP2: This overstates validation: `prerequisites[].profiles` is not checked, so an unknown profile silently skips that diagnostic in `doctor`. Limit this claim to the reference fields the validator checks, or add the missing validation.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/configuration.md, line 28:\n\n<comment>This overstates validation: `prerequisites[].profiles` is not checked, so an unknown profile silently skips that diagnostic in `doctor`. Limit this claim to the reference fields the validator checks, or add the missing validation.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@\n+| `environmentOutputs` | no | Repository-relative dotenv or JSON runtime files and owner-only permission modes. |\n+| `policy` | no | Repository-relative organization policy JSON path. |\n+\n+Every repository-relative path rejects absolute paths, `..` escape, and runtime symlink escape. References to ports, processes, services, profiles, dependencies, and hostname targets must resolve during validation. An explicitly configured but missing policy is an error; only the conventional unconfigured policy path is optional.\n+\n+## Ports\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\nEvery repository-relative path rejects absolute paths, `..` escape, and runtime symlink escape. References to ports, processes, services, dependencies, `defaultProfile`, hostname profile filters, and hostname targets must resolve during validation; prerequisite profile filters are not currently checked. An explicitly configured but missing policy is an error; only the conventional unconfigured policy path is optional.\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`13f5618`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/13f561830279b4c40c8d095f2fdd38ff4c719bfa)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNncu resolved=True devfn/docs/content/docs/lifecycle.md\n<!-- cubic:v=f56220e7-196c-4b7e-b6fa-b1e625c3fa04 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=ce14b52f-6485-5594-8298-c25e4d334624 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":10} -->\nP2: This overstates where runtime artifacts live: machine registry state uses the platform state directory, and configured `environmentOutputs[].path` files can be elsewhere in the repository. Name only the artifacts stored under `runtimeDir` and call out those separate locations so users can find and clean up state safely.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At devfn/docs/content/docs/lifecycle.md, line 10:\n\n<comment>This overstates where runtime artifacts live: machine registry state uses the platform state directory, and configured `environmentOutputs[].path` files can be elsewhere in the repository. Name only the artifacts stored under `runtimeDir` and call out those separate locations so users can find and clean up state safely.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@\n+\n+`devfn up` plans resources in dependency order, reserves ports before mutation, starts selected native processes and Compose services, verifies readiness, registers proxy routes, and returns a machine-readable receipt. If an invocation fails, rollback targets resources created by that invocation. `status`, `logs`, and `doctor` expose live state and diagnostics; `down` stops only the exact worktree instance.\n+\n+There is no background daemon in version 0.1. State, journals, logs, and generated environment files are kept under the configured runtime directory, `.devfn/` by default. Process ownership uses a PID birth signature where the host supplies one, so cleanup refuses a reused PID.\n+\n+Ordinary `down` does not delete persistent Docker volumes. It is also not a general reset command. Explicit configured environment outputs may have overwritten files that existed before adoption; inspect them before manual cleanup. The [core package](/docs/reference/core), [process supervisor](/docs/reference/processes), and [migration guide](/docs/reference/migration) describe lifecycle boundaries.\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\nThere is no background daemon in version 0.1. Project receipts, journals, and logs are kept under the configured runtime directory, `.devfn/` by default; machine registry state uses the platform state directory, and configured environment outputs may be written elsewhere in the repository. Process ownership uses a PID birth signature where the host supplies one, so cleanup refuses a reused PID.\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`13f5618`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/13f561830279b4c40c8d095f2fdd38ff4c719bfa)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNncv resolved=True devfn/docs/README.md\n<!-- cubic:v=128b4c96-8b66-4131-9b8a-b01ecd6330fa -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=ce14b52f-6485-5594-8298-c25e4d334624 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} -->\nP2: The validation command cannot find the locally installed `docsfn` binary in a normal shell. Invoke it through `npx` so the workspace-local CLI runs.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At devfn/docs/README.md, line 12:\n\n<comment>The validation command cannot find the locally installed `docsfn` binary in a normal shell. Invoke it through `npx` so the workspace-local CLI runs.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@\n+npm --workspace @devfn/docs run build\n+```\n+\n+The build regenerates `static/llms.txt` and `static/llms-full.txt`. Run `docsfn validate --root .` from `devfn/docs`. The site defaults to port 6017. Set `site.canonicalUrl` in `docsfn.config.ts` after the public host is assigned.\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`13f5618`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/13f561830279b4c40c8d095f2fdd38ff4c719bfa)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNncy resolved=True devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/security.md\n<!-- cubic:v=5b917587-442f-45c6-ad8a-57a0c8ed2280 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=ce14b52f-6485-5594-8298-c25e4d334624 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} -->\nP2: The lifecycle receipt serializes each managed process's `command` verbatim, so credentials passed as command arguments are persisted despite this guarantee. Limit the claim to `secretEnv` values and warn against embedding credentials in arguments.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/security.md, line 9:\n\n<comment>The lifecycle receipt serializes each managed process's `command` verbatim, so credentials passed as command arguments are persisted despite this guarantee. Limit the claim to `secretEnv` values and warn against embedding credentials in arguments.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@\n+# DevFn security\n+\n+- Every DevFn manifest can declare lifecycle commands, so the CLI refuses to load JSON, TypeScript, or JavaScript until the user records trust for its exact digest with `--trust`. JSON is parsed directly from the verified bytes; executable manifests run from a private copy of those same bytes and must be self-contained, with imports and `require()` rejected so dependency files cannot bypass the digest boundary.\n+- Runtime children inherit a small base environment plus explicit `envAllowlist` entries. Sensitive-looking keys must also be listed in `secretEnv`; a detached wrapper redacts those effective values before native-process logs are persisted. Literal values are rejected only when their key looks sensitive, so review every manifest literal. Compose logging is disabled for services with `secretEnv` because Docker otherwise retains historical unredacted logs. Secrets are not persisted in the registry or lifecycle receipt.\n+- Generated environment and state files use owner-only modes (default `0600`); their directories use `0700`. Existing files are explicitly re-permissioned after each write.\n+- Local ports and proxy targets bind to loopback unless a manifest explicitly selects public exposure. Profiles containing public processes or ports require the separate `--allow-public` confirmation on every start. A public Cloudflare tunnel must never be inferred.\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`13f5618`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/13f561830279b4c40c8d095f2fdd38ff4c719bfa)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNnc1 resolved=True devfn/docs/src/routes/+layout.server.ts\n<!-- cubic:v=bd00d907-64bf-41ee-8301-03486b6b0eaa -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=ce14b52f-6485-5594-8298-c25e4d334624 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} -->\nP2: Returning the full `source` sends every documentation page and the search artifact in the layout payload, even on routes that only need the site configuration. Return only client-needed layout fields and keep manifest/search processing server-side; the search artifact is already fetched separately.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At devfn/docs/src/routes/+layout.server.ts, line 6:\n\n<comment>Returning the full `source` sends every documentation page and the search artifact in the layout payload, even on routes that only need the site configuration. Return only client-needed layout fields and keep manifest/search processing server-side; the search artifact is already fetched separately.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@\n+\n+export const load: LayoutServerLoad = async () => {\n+  return {\n+    source: await loadDocsSiteSource(),\n+  };\n+};\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`aabb7d6`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/aabb7d6f0d3147d010d061f4a461ff1ba6d059a8)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNnc4 resolved=True devfn/docs/static/llms.txt\n<!-- cubic:v=5638b8b1-1b08-4013-bf6f-aa991a899023 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=ce14b52f-6485-5594-8298-c25e4d334624 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP3: The generated `llms.txt` links are origin-relative (`/docs/configuration`) because `site.canonicalUrl` is not set in `devfn/docs/docsfn.config.ts` — unlike authfn's docs site, which emits absolute URLs. Once committed and fetched by LLM clients, these paths have no resolvable host. Set `canonicalUrl` in the site config and regenerate the artifacts (via `npm --workspace @devfn/docs run generate:llms`), or hold off committing llms.txt until the public host is assigned.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At devfn/docs/static/llms.txt, line 7:\n\n<comment>The generated `llms.txt` links are origin-relative (`/docs/configuration`) because `site.canonicalUrl` is not set in `devfn/docs/docsfn.config.ts` — unlike authfn's docs site, which emits absolute URLs. Once committed and fetched by LLM clients, these paths have no resolvable host. Set `canonicalUrl` in the site config and regenerate the artifacts (via `npm --workspace @devfn/docs run generate:llms`), or hold off committing llms.txt until the public host is assigned.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@\n+\n+## Documentation\n+\n+- [Configuration](/docs/configuration) — Declare project identity, ports, processes, Compose services, and profiles.\n+- [Getting started](/docs/getting-started) — Initialize, trust, inspect, and start a local profile.\n+- [DevFn](/docs) — Trusted lifecycle orchestration for local development.\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`2fcf415`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/2fcf4157333b08d1c68a79cefb3a667bbfe642cc)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNnc8 resolved=True devfn/docs/src/routes/docs/[...slug]/+page.server.ts\n<!-- cubic:v=555d6181-0d4c-4b46-ac96-08acaf7504a6 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=ce14b52f-6485-5594-8298-c25e4d334624 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":6} -->\nP3: This API branch hardcodes `sidebarId: \"api\"`, but devfn's docsfn.config.ts only defines the `docs` sidebar, so `manifest.sidebars[\"api\"]` is undefined and API pages would render without the sidebar. Either add an `api` sidebar to docsfn.config.ts (as authfn/docs does) or drop the unused API branch.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At devfn/docs/src/routes/docs/[...slug]/+page.server.ts, line 65:\n\n<comment>This API branch hardcodes `sidebarId: \"api\"`, but devfn's docsfn.config.ts only defines the `docs` sidebar, so `manifest.sidebars[\"api\"]` is undefined and API pages would render without the sidebar. Either add an `api` sidebar to docsfn.config.ts (as authfn/docs does) or drop the unused API branch.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,120 @@\n+        typeof api.frontmatter.description === \"string\" ? api.frontmatter.description : undefined,\n+      canonicalPath: route,\n+      canonicalUrl: buildCanonicalUrl(source.canonicalUrl, route),\n+      sidebarId: \"api\",\n+      headings: [],\n+      breadcrumbs: [\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`13f5618`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/13f561830279b4c40c8d095f2fdd38ff4c719bfa)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNp6K resolved=True devfn/docs/package.json\n**Security issue**  \n🛑 Blocker — must fix before merge\n\n**Known vulnerabilities in svelte@5.0.0**\n\nOSV.dev reports 6 known vulnerabilities affecting `svelte@5.0.0`, introduced by this PR:\n\n- [GHSA-crpf-4hrx-3jrp](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-27125) **moderate**: Svelte SSR attribute spreading includes inherited properties from prototype chain — fixed in 5.51.5\n- [GHSA-f7gr-6p89-r883](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-27121) **moderate**: Svelte affected by cross-site scripting via spread attributes in Svelte SSR — fixed in 5.51.5\n- [GHSA-m56q-vw4c-c2cp](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-27122) **moderate**: Svelte SSR does not validate dynamic element tag names in `<svelte:element>` — fixed in 5.51.5\n\n…and 3 more — see the OSV links above.\n\nUpgrade to 5.51.5 or later.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn devfn/docs/package.json, upgrade the dependency svelte from 5.0.0 to a non-vulnerable version (5.51.5, 5.53.5, 5.55.7). Update any associated lockfile entries.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n> Not useful? Reply `@mira-rhombus reject` to dismiss this suggestion.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNp6O resolved=True devfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts\n**Refactor suggestion**  \n⚠️ Warning\n\n**Missing test coverage**\n\nThe PR introduces non-trivial logic across the new site — the bundled content provider, the hand-rolled `parseFrontmatter`, per-collection entry filtering, compiled-cache keying/lookup, and the route-resolution helpers in `docs/[...slug]/+page.server.ts` — but ships no test files, and the package's `test` script is `vitest run --passWithNoTests`, so zero assertions guard this code. At minimum, cover `parseFrontmatter` edge cases (missing closing fence, CRLF input, quoted values) and the collection filtering rules.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn the devfn/docs package, add a Vitest suite (for example src/lib/server/docs-site-source.test.ts and a companion file for src/routes/docs/[...slug]/+page.server.ts) covering parseFrontmatter edge cases (missing closing fence, CRLF frontmatter, quoted/unquoted values, boolean coercion), collectEntriesForCollection filtering (.gitkeep, meta.json, per-collection extensions), getCompiledArtifactOrThrow missing-key errors, and the route helpers buildCanonicalUrl, isRouteNotFoundError, and hasNestedDocsRoutes; wire the tests so `npm test` actually executes them instead of relying on --passWithNoTests.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n> Not useful? Reply `@mira-rhombus reject` to dismiss this suggestion.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNp6R resolved=True devfn/docs/src/routes/docs/[...slug]/+page.server.ts\n**Error Handling**  \n⚠️ Warning\n\n**Type guard claims message without checking it**\n\nThe predicate type `input is { message: string }` promises a string `message`, but the check only inspects `code`. Any `DOCS_ROUTE_NOT_FOUND`-coded object whose `message` is missing or non-string passes the guard, and the catch block below then forwards a non-string to SvelteKit's `error(404, routeError.message)`. Verify `message` as part of the predicate.\n\n```suggestion\nfunction isRouteNotFoundError(input: unknown): input is { message: string } {\n  return (\n    typeof input === \"object\" &&\n    input !== null &&\n    \"code\" in input &&\n    String((input as { code: unknown }).code) === \"DOCS_ROUTE_NOT_FOUND\" &&\n    \"message\" in input &&\n    typeof (input as { message: unknown }).message === \"string\"\n  );\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn devfn/docs/src/routes/docs/[...slug]/+page.server.ts, update the isRouteNotFoundError guard (lines 22-30) to also verify that `message` exists and is a string before narrowing to { message: string } — e.g. add `\"message\" in input && typeof (input as { message: unknown }).message === \"string\"` — so error(404, routeError.message) never receives an undefined or non-string message.\n\nApply this code change:\n\nfunction isRouteNotFoundError(input: unknown): input is { message: string } {\n  return (\n    typeof input === \"object\" &&\n    input !== null &&\n    \"code\" in input &&\n    String((input as { code: unknown }).code) === \"DOCS_ROUTE_NOT_FOUND\" &&\n    \"message\" in input &&\n    typeof (input as { message: unknown }).message === \"string\"\n  );\n}\n```\n\n</details>\n\n> Not useful? Reply `@mira-rhombus reject` to dismiss this suggestion.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNtlZ resolved=True devfn/docs/content/docs/getting-started.md\nOn a fresh project, this `init` call only prints a preview; it does not create `devfn.config.ts`, so the following `doctor --trust` fails with no manifest. Please show the required review-and-rerun step with `init --yes` before `doctor`, and align the CLI reference example.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Fresh-start command sequence does not create a manifest\n\n## Affected sites\n- `devfn/docs/content/docs/getting-started.md:11-12` — command sequence previews, then attempts to load a missing manifest.\n- `devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/cli.md:11-13` — includes both forms but does not explain that the first only previews.\n- `devfn/cli/src/index.ts:124-135` — `init` returns `written: false` unless `--yes` is supplied.\n\n## Required outcome\n- A user following the getting-started commands after reviewing the preview can create a manifest before running `doctor --trust`.\n````\n\n</details>\nAddressed in aabb7d6: the getting-started flow now reruns `init --yes` after reviewing the preview, and the CLI reference includes both commands.\n\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\n<sup><a href=\"https://pullfrog.com\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\"><img src=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\" width=\"9px\" height=\"9px\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; \" alt=\"Pullfrog\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/36218761149/job/108339905449) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNtlh resolved=True devfn/docs/src/lib/components/DocsSiteSearch.svelte\nIf this site is deployed via the repository's Cloudflare docs convention, the Worker is routed only under `/docs*`, while this request goes to `/search.json` at the host root. The origin then handles the request instead of the docs Worker, so search fails; place the endpoint and fetch URL inside the docs route scope before enabling that deployment. No DevFn host is registered yet, so this is a deployment-readiness issue.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Search artifact misses the Cloudflare docs Worker\n\n## Affected sites\n- `devfn/docs/src/lib/components/DocsSiteSearch.svelte:5` — fetches the host-root search artifact.\n- `devfn/docs/src/routes/search.json/+server.ts:5` — serves an endpoint outside the `/docs*` route.\n- `scripts/cloudflare-docs/config.mjs:106` — current documentation Workers bind to `host/docs*` only.\n\n## Required outcome\n- When the new site is deployed under the repository's docs route convention, its search request resolves to the Worker that serves its search artifact.\n````\n\n</details>\nAddressed in 13f5618: search now fetches `/docs/search.json`, and the endpoint is served under `/docs`.\n\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\n<sup><a href=\"https://pullfrog.com\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\"><img src=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\" width=\"9px\" height=\"9px\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; \" alt=\"Pullfrog\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/36233435883/job/108380780682) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNznn resolved=False scripts/docs-site/Search.svelte\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Keep the search request under the deployed route**\n\n[391 more lines in file. Use offset=451 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791221079982}}
