{"type":"message","id":"6a068866","parentId":"1d61dc12","timestamp":"2026-10-05T17:24:49.080Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_RRwb0E393H5BvX5IWb8Ztz56|fc_055fb762f51dfcfc016ac3dd5fcf4887d0979f22e65db66ae9","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\nWhen this site is deployed through the repository's Cloudflare docs mechanism, `scripts/cloudflare-docs/config.mjs` attaches each docs worker only to `${host}/docs*`, so this root-level `/search.json` request bypasses the worker and search returns an error. Serve the endpoint below `/docs` (and fetch that URL), or explicitly include `/search.json` in the worker routes.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNzno resolved=False devfn/docs/content/docs/lifecycle.md\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Document the machine state directory separately**\n\nThis says state is kept under the configured project runtime directory, but `defaultStateDir()` stores trust records, the port registry, lifecycle locks, and proxy state under `$XDG_STATE_HOME/devfn` (or `~/.local/state/devfn`); only receipts, logs, and generated runtime outputs default to `.devfn/`. Users following this lifecycle or cleanup guidance could therefore overlook the actual machine-level state.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNzuS resolved=True devfn/docs/vite.config.ts\n<!-- cubic:v=bdece536-ef0f-460a-9815-90d65c1efddb -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=f4cc99c8-3960-547f-8e8d-14a5e399afc4 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":8} -->\nP2: `import.meta.resolve` is unavailable without a flag on Node 18.17–18.18, but the repository supports `>=18.17.0`; Vite config evaluation therefore fails before the site can start or build on those versions. Use Node-18.17-compatible package resolution or raise the supported minimum.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At devfn/docs/vite.config.ts, line 22:\n\n<comment>`import.meta.resolve` is unavailable without a flag on Node 18.17–18.18, but the repository supports `>=18.17.0`; Vite config evaluation therefore fails before the site can start or build on those versions. Use Node-18.17-compatible package resolution or raise the supported minimum.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -18,6 +18,9 @@ export default defineConfig({\n   resolve: {\n     alias: [\n+      // Resolve shared source against this site's pinned DocsFn installation.\n+      { find: /^@docsfn\\/core$/, replacement: fileURLToPath(import.meta.resolve(\"@docsfn/core\")) },\n+      { find: \"@docsfn/core/search-runtime\", replacement: fileURLToPath(import.meta.resolve(\"@docsfn/core/search-runtime\")) },\n       { find: \"@searchfn/client\", replacement: path.resolve(dirname, \"../../searchfn/client/src/index.ts\") },\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`13f5618`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/13f561830279b4c40c8d095f2fdd38ff4c719bfa)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNzuU resolved=True scripts/docs-site/README.md\n<!-- cubic:v=642b632c-ef34-45cc-934d-f67f948884ae -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=f4cc99c8-3960-547f-8e8d-14a5e399afc4 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} -->\nP2: AuthFn and FileFn still use independent runtime copies, so edits here will not update all sites as this guidance implies. Migrate those consumers or clarify that this shared runtime currently serves DevFn only.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At scripts/docs-site/README.md, line 9:\n\n<comment>AuthFn and FileFn still use independent runtime copies, so edits here will not update all sites as this guidance implies. Migrate those consumers or clarify that this shared runtime currently serves DevFn only.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@\n+\n+Each site resolves the shared module's DocsFn imports through its own Vite aliases so it uses the versions pinned by that site. Run `npm run build` in the affected `<function>/docs` directory. After changing shared code, build all consumers and verify desktop search (including a result navigation and Escape) plus the mobile Menu drawer. Keep the responsive open-drawer override when using the current published theme.\n+\n+The new-site PRs carry identical copies of this shared directory so they can land independently. Once merged, edits belong here rather than in the small per-site factory wrappers.\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`13f5618`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/13f561830279b4c40c8d095f2fdd38ff4c719bfa)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mNzuV resolved=True scripts/docs-site/runtime.ts\n<!-- cubic:v=d5b94b80-a8d5-4cfa-9a9e-27e811c8f686 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=f4cc99c8-3960-547f-8e8d-14a5e399afc4 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} -->\nP2: `parseFrontmatter` skips CRLF-frontmatter because it only recognizes `---\\n`; the YAML then renders as body content and its metadata is lost. Accept `\\r?\\n` after the opening delimiter.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At scripts/docs-site/runtime.ts, line 481:\n\n<comment>`parseFrontmatter` skips CRLF-frontmatter because it only recognizes `---\\n`; the YAML then renders as body content and its metadata is lost. Accept `\\r?\\n` after the opening delimiter.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -0,0 +1,537 @@\n+  body: string;\n+  frontmatter: Record<string, unknown>;\n+} {\n+  if (!source.startsWith(\"---\\n\")) {\n+    return { body: source, frontmatter: {} };\n+  }\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\n  if (!/^---\\r?\\n/.test(source)) {\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`13f5618`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/13f561830279b4c40c8d095f2fdd38ff4c719bfa)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mPowm resolved=False scripts/docs-site/layout.ts\n## Superfluous trailing arguments\n\n<p>Superfluous argument passed to <a class=\"Link\" href=\"/21nCo/super-functions/blob/13f561830279b4c40c8d095f2fdd38ff4c719bfa/scripts/verify-uifn-react-18-runtime.mjs#L49-L49\">default constructor of anonymous class</a>.</p>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mPo2R resolved=True devfn/docs/src/routes/docs/[...slug]/+page.server.ts\n![kody code-review](https://img.shields.io/badge/kody-code--review-312B4B?labelColor=C9BBF2) ![Kody Rules](https://img.shields.io/badge/Kody_Rules-4527A0) ![medium](https://img.shields.io/badge/severity_level-medium-1A7BBE)\n\n\nImplicit `any` type on the `let routeEntry;` declaration violates Rule [2], which disallows `any` because it defeats TypeScript's strict type-checking and can hide runtime errors. Annotate the declaration with `ReturnType<typeof resolveDocsRouteDataOrThrow>`, or restructure the code to assign a properly typed value directly.\n\nKody rule violation: [Disallow \\`any\\` type usage](https://app.kodus.io/settings/code-review/global/kody-rules/5ba5ce8d-2e90-425b-8ca3-6019f927f489?teamId=c7d4a17c-c2c8-426a-9c23-3048fd1d53b9)\n\n```typescript\nlet routeEntry: ReturnType<typeof resolveDocsRouteDataOrThrow>;\n```\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Prompt for LLM</summary>\n\n```\n\nFile devfn/docs/src/routes/docs/[...slug]/+page.server.ts:\n\nLine 40:\n\nImplicit `any` type on the `let routeEntry;` declaration violates Rule [2], which disallows `any` because it defeats TypeScript's strict type-checking and can hide runtime errors. Annotate the declaration with `ReturnType<typeof resolveDocsRouteDataOrThrow>`, or restructure the code to assign a properly typed value directly.\n\nSuggested Code:\n\nlet routeEntry: ReturnType<typeof resolveDocsRouteDataOrThrow>;\n\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n<sub>Talk to Kody by mentioning @kody</sub>\n\n\n<sub>Was this suggestion helpful? React with 👍 or 👎 to help Kody learn from this interaction.</sub>\n\n<!-- kody-codereview -->&#8203;\n&#8203;\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mPqSc resolved=False devfn/docs/package.json\n**Security issue**  \n🛑 Blocker — must fix before merge\n\n**Known vulnerabilities in vite@5.4.0**\n\nOSV.dev reports 15 known vulnerabilities affecting `vite@5.4.0`, introduced by this PR:\n\n- [GHSA-356w-63v5-8wf4](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-32395) **moderate**: Vite has an `server.fs.deny` bypass with an invalid `request-target` — fixed in 6.2.6, 6.1.5, 6.0.15, 5.4.18, 4.5.13\n- [GHSA-4r4m-qw57-chr8](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-31125) **moderate**: Vite has a `server.fs.deny` bypassed for `inline` and `raw` with `?import` query — fixed in 6.2.4, 6.1.3, 6.0.13, 5.4.16, 4.5.11\n- [GHSA-4w7w-66w2-5vf9](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-39365) **moderate**: Vite Vulnerable to Path Traversal in Optimized Deps `.map` Handling — fixed in 8.0.5, 7.3.2, 6.4.2\n\n…and 12 more — see the OSV links above.\n\nUpgrade to 6.2.6, 6.1.5, 6.0.15, 5.4.18, 4.5.13 or later.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn devfn/docs/package.json, upgrade the dependency vite from 5.4.0 to a non-vulnerable version (0.1.24, 2.14.1, 2.9.0, 3.2.11, 4.5.10, 4.5.11, 4.5.12, 4.5.13, 4.5.14, 4.5.4, 4.5.6, 5.2.14, 5.3.6, 5.4.12, 5.4.15, 5.4.16, 5.4.17, 5.4.18, 5.4.19, 5.4.20, 5.4.21, 5.4.6, 5.4.9, 6.0.12, 6.0.13, 6.0.14, 6.0.15, 6.0.9, 6.1.2, 6.1.3, 6.1.4, 6.1.5, 6.1.6, 6.2.3, 6.2.4, 6.2.5, 6.2.6, 6.2.7, 6.3.4, 6.3.6, 6.4.1, 6.4.2, 6.4.3, 7.0.7, 7.0.8, 7.1.11, 7.1.5, 7.3.2, 7.3.5, 8.0.16, 8.0.5). Update any associated lockfile entries.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n> Not useful? Reply `@mira-rhombus reject` to dismiss this suggestion.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mP2wk resolved=False devfn/docs/package.json\n**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Register DevFn with the docs deployment pipeline**\n\nThe new `@devfn/docs` workspace cannot be deployed by the repository's Cloudflare docs tooling: `scripts/cloudflare-docs/config.mjs` has no `devfn` product, `select-products.mjs` never selects changes under `devfn/docs`, and the deploy workflow neither watches that directory nor offers DevFn as a product. Confirmed by running `node scripts/cloudflare-docs/deploy.mjs dev --products=devfn --dry-run --skip-build`, which exits with `Invalid docs product: devfn`; register the product and add the corresponding workflow paths/options so this site can reach its documented public URL.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mP28x resolved=False devfn/docs/package.json\n**Security issue**  \n🛑 Blocker — must fix before merge\n\n**Known vulnerabilities in vite@5.4.0**\n\nOSV.dev reports 15 known vulnerabilities affecting `vite@5.4.0`, introduced by this PR:\n\n- [GHSA-356w-63v5-8wf4](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-32395) **moderate**: Vite has an `server.fs.deny` bypass with an invalid `request-target` — fixed in 6.2.6, 6.1.5, 6.0.15, 5.4.18, 4.5.13\n- [GHSA-4r4m-qw57-chr8](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-31125) **moderate**: Vite has a `server.fs.deny` bypassed for `inline` and `raw` with `?import` query — fixed in 6.2.4, 6.1.3, 6.0.13, 5.4.16, 4.5.11\n- [GHSA-4w7w-66w2-5vf9](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-39365) **moderate**: Vite Vulnerable to Path Traversal in Optimized Deps `.map` Handling — fixed in 8.0.5, 7.3.2, 6.4.2\n\n…and 12 more — see the OSV links above.\n\nUpgrade to 6.2.6, 6.1.5, 6.0.15, 5.4.18, 4.5.13 or later.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn devfn/docs/package.json, upgrade the dependency vite from 5.4.0 to a non-vulnerable version (0.1.24, 2.14.1, 2.9.0, 3.2.11, 4.5.10, 4.5.11, 4.5.12, 4.5.13, 4.5.14, 4.5.4, 4.5.6, 5.2.14, 5.3.6, 5.4.12, 5.4.15, 5.4.16, 5.4.17, 5.4.18, 5.4.19, 5.4.20, 5.4.21, 5.4.6, 5.4.9, 6.0.12, 6.0.13, 6.0.14, 6.0.15, 6.0.9, 6.1.2, 6.1.3, 6.1.4, 6.1.5, 6.1.6, 6.2.3, 6.2.4, 6.2.5, 6.2.6, 6.2.7, 6.3.4, 6.3.6, 6.4.1, 6.4.2, 6.4.3, 7.0.7, 7.0.8, 7.1.11, 7.1.5, 7.3.2, 7.3.5, 8.0.16, 8.0.5). Update any associated lockfile entries.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n> Not useful? Reply `@mira-rhombus reject` to dismiss this suggestion.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6mTTI4 resolved=True devfn/docs/src/routes/docs/[...slug]/+page.server.ts\n![kody code-review](https://img.shields.io/badge/kody-code--review-312B4B?labelColor=C9BBF2) ![Kody Rules](https://img.shields.io/badge/Kody_Rules-4527A0) ![medium](https://img.shields.io/badge/severity_level-medium-1A7BBE)\n\n\nImplicit `any` type on `let routeEntry;` violates Rule [2], defeating TypeScript's strict type-checking and potentially hiding runtime errors. Annotate the declaration with `ReturnType<typeof resolveDocsRouteDataOrThrow>` or restructure so the value is assigned in a single properly typed statement.\n\nKody rule violation: [Disallow \\`any\\` type usage](https://app.kodus.io/settings/code-review/global/kody-rules/5ba5ce8d-2e90-425b-8ca3-6019f927f489?teamId=c7d4a17c-c2c8-426a-9c23-3048fd1d53b9)\n\n```typescript\nlet routeEntry: ReturnType<typeof resolveDocsRouteDataOrThrow>;\n```\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Prompt for LLM</summary>\n\n```\n\nFile devfn/docs/src/routes/docs/[...slug]/+page.server.ts:\n\nLine 40:\n\nImplicit `any` type on `let routeEntry;` violates Rule [2], defeating TypeScript's strict type-checking and potentially hiding runtime errors. Annotate the declaration with `ReturnType<typeof resolveDocsRouteDataOrThrow>` or restructure so the value is assigned in a single properly typed statement.\n\nSuggested Code:\n\nlet routeEntry: ReturnType<typeof resolveDocsRouteDataOrThrow>;\n\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n<sub>Talk to Kody by mentioning @kody</sub>\n\n\n<sub>Was this suggestion helpful? React with 👍 or 👎 to help Kody learn from this interaction.</sub>\n\n<!-- kody-codereview -->&#8203;\n&#8203;\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6nFoqb resolved=False .github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-deploy.yml\n**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Add DevFn to the route-sync workflow**\n\nSelecting this new DevFn deployment option only uploads the Worker; `deploy.mjs` does not attach the `devfn.com/docs*` route. Fresh evidence from the repo-wide workflow search is that `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-routes.yml` remains the route-provisioning mechanism, but its product choices and zone-ID environment variables omit DevFn, so operators cannot sync this product independently and the public route can remain unattached unless they resync every product via `all` or run the script manually.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6nFrGA resolved=True scripts/cloudflare-docs/config.mjs\nThe deploy workflow now uploads the DevFn Worker, but it never creates the `dev.devfn.com/docs*` or `devfn.com/docs*` routes. The separate route-sync workflow has neither a `devfn` product choice nor a DevFn zone ID, so deploying this new product does not make its docs reachable through the normal product-specific workflows.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# DevFn Worker routes are not provisioned\n\n## Affected sites\n- `scripts/cloudflare-docs/config.mjs:8-16` — defines the new host/zone and expected Worker routes.\n- `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-deploy.yml:115-119` — calls `deploy.mjs` only, which uploads the Worker but does not call `sync-routes.mjs`.\n- `.github/workflows/superfunctions-docs-cloudflare-routes.yml:14-19,43-50` — excludes DevFn from the dispatch options and does not pass `CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID_DEVFN_COM`.\n\n## Required outcome\n- Provide an explicit route-provisioning path for both DevFn environments, with access to the DevFn Cloudflare zone, so the published `/docs*` URLs bind to the newly deployed Workers.\n````\n\n</details>\nAddressed in 261b6de: the route-sync workflow now offers DevFn and passes its zone ID for both environments.\n\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\n<sup><a href=\"https://pullfrog.com\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\"><img src=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\" width=\"9px\" height=\"9px\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; \" alt=\"Pullfrog\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/36612051725/job/109555667994) ｜ via [Pullfrog](https://pullfrog.com) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6nPZFZ resolved=True devfn/docs/src/app.html\n<!-- cubic:v=072cea6b-2701-4201-b3f2-6f48c5d8cf7a -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=c5b8f765-eab9-5ac6-b5c9-8c3966c37bdd -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":9} -->\nP2: This title appears before the route-specific title injected by `%sveltekit.head%`, so docs pages keep “DevFn docs” as their browser-tab title instead of showing the page title. Remove this static title and provide the fallback in the landing route or layout.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At devfn/docs/src/app.html, line 5:\n\n<comment>This title appears before the route-specific title injected by `%sveltekit.head%`, so docs pages keep “DevFn docs” as their browser-tab title instead of showing the page title. Remove this static title and provide the fallback in the landing route or layout.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@\n <html lang=\"en\">\n   <head>\n     <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n+    <title>DevFn docs</title>\n     <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n     %sveltekit.head%\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n✅ Addressed in [`0680df1`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/0680df1ee45cd4797f574bc99489d2dc1d1532ca)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6nPZFb resolved=True scripts/docs-site/vitest.config.ts\n<!-- cubic:v=1f419780-9f83-4b9e-ba36-1549be391611 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=c5b8f765-eab9-5ac6-b5c9-8c3966c37bdd -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":10} -->\nP3: `@botfn/docs` is not a workspace, so following this recovery command still fails; use `@devfn/docs`, which runs this config.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\n\n```text\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At scripts/docs-site/vitest.config.ts, line 10:\n\n<comment>`@botfn/docs` is not a workspace, so following this recovery command still fails; use `@devfn/docs`, which runs this config.</comment>\n\n<file context>\n@@ -1,9 +1,16 @@\n+const sitePackagePath = resolve(process.cwd(), \"package.json\");\n+const sitePackage = JSON.parse(readFileSync(sitePackagePath, \"utf8\"));\n+if (!sitePackage.name?.endsWith(\"/docs\") || !sitePackage.dependencies?.[\"@docsfn/core\"]) {\n+  throw new Error(\"Run DocsFn site tests from a consuming docs workspace, for example npm test --workspace @botfn/docs\");\n+}\n+\n</file context>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```suggestion\n  throw new Error(\"Run DocsFn site tests from a consuming docs workspace, for example npm test --workspace @devfn/docs\");\n```\n\n✅ Addressed in [`0680df1`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/0680df1ee45cd4797f574bc99489d2dc1d1532ca)\n\n## PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6nkGqp resolved=False scripts/docs-site/vitest.config.ts\n![kody code-review](https://img.shields.io/badge/kody-code--review-312B4B?labelColor=C9BBF2) ![Kody Rules](https://img.shields.io/badge/Kody_Rules-4527A0) ![medium](https://img.shields.io/badge/severity_level-medium-1A7BBE)\n\n\nImplicit `any` on `sitePackage`: the variable lacks a type annotation and inherits the `any` result of `JSON.parse`. Annotate it with an explicit shape (or cast through `unknown`) to satisfy the no-`any` type-safety rule and keep type checking strict.\n\nKody rule violation: [Disallow \\`any\\` type usage](https://app.kodus.io/settings/code-review/global/kody-rules/5ba5ce8d-2e90-425b-8ca3-6019f927f489?teamId=c7d4a17c-c2c8-426a-9c23-3048fd1d53b9)\n\n```typescript\nlet sitePackage: { name?: string; dependencies?: Record<st