->\n\n## 5324703418 pullfrog[bot]\n\n\n## 5324714935 pullfrog[bot]\n> ℹ️ No new issues found in this delta. The earlier Cloudflare search-routing thread remains open, so this is not an approval.\n\n**Reviewed changes** I reviewed the follow-up commit's navigation, search, server-loader, shared-runtime, and consumer-guidance changes against the full PR.\n\n- **Clarified initialization:** Added the `init --yes` step after previewing the generated manifest, resolving the fresh-start sequence.\n- **Adjusted site navigation:** Added a mobile sidebar override and replaced the hydration-gated search trigger with a native-dialog search component.\n- **Extracted the runtime:** Moved the manifest, search-index, and compiled-content cache into a per-site shared factory while limiting layout data to site metadata.\n- **Pinned shared imports:** Added Vite aliases so the shared code resolves DocsFn against this site's installation.\n\nLocal build and tests were not run because `npm ci` failed: the root lockfile is missing turbo platform packages.\n\n<!--\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against aabb7d6f;\nif commits have landed on codex/docs-devfn-20260926 since, treat every specific bug, file, or\nline callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it.\n\n- Mode: IncrementalReview (delta against prior pullfrog review)\n- Files reviewed: 52\n- Commits reviewed: 2\n- Base: dev (7c6ec512)\n- Head: codex/docs-devfn-20260926 (aabb7d6f)\n- Reviewed commits:\n  - b84bae1b — docs(devfn): add DocsFn consumer site\n  - aabb7d6f — docs(devfn): fix site navigation and consumer guidance\n- Prior pullfrog review: b84bae1b (https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/212#pullrequestreview-5324578247)\n-->\n\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\n<sup><a href=\"https://pullfrog.com\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\"><img src=\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full