nceDiagram\n    participant Browser\n    participant SvelteKit\n    participant Source as DocsSiteSource\n    participant DocsFn as DocsFnCore\n    participant Content as BundledContent\n\n    Browser->>SvelteKit: GET /docs/{slug}\n    SvelteKit->>Source: loadDocsSiteSource()\n    Source->>Content: load bundled content\n    Content-->>Source: Markdown entries\n    Source->>DocsFn: buildManifest(provider, config)\n    DocsFn-->>Source: manifest and routes\n    Source->>DocsFn: buildSearchIndex(manifest)\n    DocsFn-->>Source: search artifact\n    SvelteKit->>Source: getCompiledDocsPage(pageId)\n    Source->>DocsFn: compileSvelteContent(source)\n    DocsFn-->>Source: compiled artifact\n    SvelteKit-->>Browser: Render DocsLayout and DocsContent\n```\n\n#### Flow diagram for generating DevFn documentation indexes\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    Start[\"npm run build\"] --> Generate[\"generate-llms.mjs\"]\n    Generate --> Load[\"loadDocsConfig\"]\n    Load --> Provider[\"FsContentProvider\"]\n    Provider --> Manifest[\"buildManifest\"]\n    Manifest --> Artifacts[\"buildLlmsTxtArtifacts\"]\n    Artifacts --> Write[\"Write static/llms.txt and static/llms-full.txt\"]\n    Write --> Vite[\"vite build\"]\n```\n\n### File-Level Changes\n\n| Change | Details | Files |\n| ------ | ------- | ----- |\n| Adds a complete SvelteKit consumer documentation site for DevFn, with DocsFn-powered content discovery, rendering, navigation, search, and package/reference pages. | <ul><li>Adds consumer guides covering installation, configuration, lifecycle, packages, ports, processes, security, and migration.</li><li>Adds package-specific reference pages and a generated reference index.</li><li>Configures DocsFn metadata, navigation, sidebar, search, public access, and edit links.</li><li>Implements bundled filesystem content loading, frontmatter/control-file parsing, manifest construction, compiled-content caching, route resolution, canonical URLs, and relative-link handling.</li><li>Adds SvelteKit layouts, landing page, documentation routes, API rendering, breadcrumbs, pagination, search endpoint, and site-specific styling.</li></ul> | `devfn/docs/content/docs/**/*.md`<br/>`devfn/docs/content/docs/meta.json`<br/>`devfn/docs/content/docs/reference/meta.json`<br/>`devfn/docs/docsfn.config.ts`<br/>`devfn/docs/src/lib/server/docs-site-source.ts`<br/>`devfn/docs/src/lib/components/DocsSiteSearch.svelte`<br/>`devfn/docs/src/routes/+layout.server.ts`<br/>`devfn/docs/src/routes/+layout.svelte`<br/>`devfn/docs/src/routes/+page.server.ts`<br/>`devfn/docs/src/routes/+page.svelte`<br/>`devfn/docs/src/routes/docs/[...slug]/+page.server.ts`<br/>`devfn/docs/src/routes/docs/[...slug]/+page.svelte`<br/>`devfn/docs/src/routes/search.json/+server.ts`<br/>`devfn/docs/src/app.css`<br/>`devfn/docs/src/app.html` |\n| Adds the @devfn/docs workspace package and its local development/build toolchain. | <ul><li>Defines dev, build, preview, test, and LLMS generation scripts.</li><li>Adds DocsFn, SvelteKit, Tailwind, adapter, font, and UI dependencies.</li><li>Configures SvelteKit preprocessing, optional Cloudflare deployment mode, asset paths, and generated application directory.</li><li>Configures Vite, Tailwind, SvelteKit, SSR no-external handling, and monorepo SearchFn source aliases.</li><li>Adds TypeScript configuration and package documentation with validation/build instructions.</li></ul> | `devfn/docs/package.json`<br/>`devfn/docs/README.md`<br/>`devfn/docs/svelte.config.js`<br/>`devfn/docs/tsconfig.json`<br/>`devfn/docs/vite.config.ts`<br/>`devfn/docs/.gitignore` |\n| Generates and checks in LLM-oriented documentation indexes for the new site. | <ul><li>Builds DocsFn manifests from bundled content and writes llms.txt and llms-full.txt during prebuild.</li><li>Adds generated site artifacts for documentation consumers.</li></ul> | `devfn/docs/scripts/generate-llms.mjs`<br/>`devfn/docs/static/llms.txt`<br/>`devfn/docs/static/llms-full.txt` |\n| Integrates the documentation workspace into the repository dependency lockfile. | <ul><li>Records the new workspace package and its resolved dependency graph in the root lockfile.</li></ul> | `package-lock.json` |\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Tips and commands</summary>\n\n#### Interacting with Sourcery\n\n- **Trigger a new review:** Comment `@sourcery-ai review` on the pull request.\n- **Continue discussions:** Reply directly to Sourcery's review comments.\n- **Generate a GitHub issue from a review comment:** Ask Sourcery to create an\n  issue from a review comment by replying to it. You can also reply to a\n  review comment with `@sourcery-ai issue` to create an issue from it.\n- **Generate a pull request title:** Write `@sourcery-ai` anywhere in the pull\n  request title to generate a title at any time. You can also comment\n  `@sourcery-ai title` on the pull request to (re-)generate the title at any time.\n- **Generate a pull request summary:** Write `@sourcery-ai summary` anywhere in\n  the pull request body to generate a PR summary at any time exactly where you\n  want it. You can also comment `@sourcery-ai summary` on the pull request to\n  (re-)generate the summary at any time.\n- **Generate reviewer's guide:** Comment `@sourcery-ai guide` on the pull\n  request to (re-)generate the reviewer's guide at any time.\n- **Resolve all Sourcery comments:** Comment `@sourcery-ai resolve` on the\n  pull request to resolve all Sourcery comments. Useful if you've already\n  addressed all the comments and don't want to see them anymore.\n- **Dismiss all Sourcery reviews:** Comment `@sourcery-ai dismiss` on the pull\n  request to dismiss all existing Sourcery reviews. Especially useful if you\n  want to start fresh with a new review - don't forget to comment\n  `@sourcery-ai review` to trigger a new review!\n\n#### Customizing Your Experience\n\nAccess your [dashboard](https://app.sourcery.ai) to:\n- Enable or disable review features such as the Sourcery-generated pull request\n  summary, the reviewer's guide, and others.\n- Change the review language.\n- Add, remove or edit custom review instructions.\n- Adjust other review settings.\n\n#### Getting Help\n\n- [Contact our support team](mailto:support@sourcery.ai) for questions or feedback.\n- Visit our [documentation](https://docs.sourcery.ai) for detailed guides and information.\n- Keep in touch with the Sourcery team by following us on [X/Twitter](https://x.com/SourceryAI), [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/company/sourcery-ai/) or [GitHub](https://github.com/sourcery-ai).\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- Generated by sourcery-ai[bot]: end review_guide -->\n\n## 5843059174 kody-ai[bot]\n![kody code-review](https://img.shields.io/badge/kody-code--review-312B4B?labelColor=C9BBF2) ![Business Logic](https://img.shields.io/badge/Business_Logic-0091EA) ![medium](https://img.shields.io/badge/severity_level-medium-1A7BBE)\n\n<!-- task_context_status:weak -->\n## 🤔 Insufficient Task Context\n\nI found a task linked to this PR, but it only contains minimal information (title only, no description or acceptance criteria). To perform a meaningful business rules validation, I need more details.\n\n### 🔍 What I need to validate:\n- Business requirements and acceptance criteria\n- Expected behavior and business rules\n- Edge cases and constraints to consider\n\n### 💡 How to improve the task context:\n- Add a description to the linked ticket\n- Include acceptance criteria or business rules\n- Describe the expected behavior after the change\n\n### ⚠️ Important:\nA task title alone is not sufficient to determine whether the implementation is correct or complete.\n\n---\n> 💡 This validation runs automatically only on the first review of a pull request. To run it again, comment `@kody -v business-logic`.\n\n## 5843268316 kody-ai[bot]\n## Code Review Could Not Complete ⚠️\n\nThe review failed before suggestions could be generated.\n\n**Reason:** The configured API key (open_router) is out of credits or has hit its billing limit. Top 