ative interfaces stay intact.\nFaithful boundary: pristine native preview served both files200 with correct text MIME and exact generated bytes in all3 root consumers, but the genuine corpus contained7 obsolete `https://authfn.superfunctions.dev/llms...` references sourced from5 exact-base AuthFn AI docs. `final212-root-native-text-http.log` failed its content assertion, retained. This is not a transport failure and not a live-host test. Native/source reading traces each originating file. The old guide also advertises nonexistent docs:llms/llmsTxt options, unsupported corpus/size guarantees and wrong default port.\nOwnership plan: selectively reuse exact previously reviewed4e67 five AuthFn AI docs (four single URL replacements plus corrected llms-txt guide), read the158-line proposed diff; this is the same affected AuthFn producer/public-origin family, not CliFn/BotFn transfer or broad URL normalization. Do not touch other homepage/default-base documents. Archive/hash/mode verify all5 current files in root+existing genuine AuthFn context before writes; apply exact content, record explicit source-plan supplement, ordinary producer/prebuild regenerates owned AuthFn artifacts. Prior immutable158 plan remains historical; final scope must include5 paths and generated afterimages rather than falsely claiming unchanged-plan capture.\nIndependent acceptance: actual script/declaration6005/published includeBlog:false/config/consumer prerequisite contracts already traced; regenerate/rebuild Root+genuine AuthFn, checks/tests/types/native preview exact bytes/MIME and absence of these obsolete references; read final generated source diff. Preserve all earlier failures/qualified gaps. No live hosting/domain/registry/secrets/thread operation; publication/final canonical/protected/ancestry gates remain closed.\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","usage":{"input":1915,"output":1519,"cacheRead":137088,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1034,"to